//? Title: Hopcroft–Karp: shortest augmentations and a matching certificate
//? Subtitle: Actual BFS labels, path flips, a cutoff correction and an explicit DFS stack
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Match as many eligible left/right pairs as possible while using each vertex at
most once. Hopcroft–Karp groups shortest augmenting paths into blocking phases.
This report begins with a two-pair rematching, retains the original
five-applicant/four-job graph, and follows actual BFS labels and path stacks
from the producing C++ kernel. A six-by-six counterexample explains why its
former DFS needed a shortest-path cutoff. An explicit stack handles long paths,
while a minimum vertex cover from the terminal BFS independently certifies
optimal cardinality. Selected visit counters describe work without substituting
theoretical curves for measurements.
)

\toc

> Rematch one pair to gain another

Use edges L0–R0, L0–R1 and L1–R0 in that order. The first phase matches L0 to
R0. L1 cannot take the occupied R0 directly. In the next phase, its actual
augmenting path is L1, R0, L0, R1: insert L1–R0, remove L0–R0, insert L0–R1. Two
forward unmatched edges and one backward matched edge gain exactly one pair.

The following program displays that actual path before its producing flip. Trace
phases include the final unsuccessful BFS; a shortest-pair count of zero denotes
that terminal record, not a zero-length augmentation.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hopcroft_karp_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/hopcroft_karp_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto t =
        dm::algorithms::hopcroft_karp_trace(2, 2, {{0, 0}, {0, 1}, {1, 0}});
    std::print("| BFS call | shortest forward pairs | actual augmentations |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &phase : t.phases)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", phase.bfs_index, phase.shortest_pairs,
                   phase.augmentations.size());
    const auto &path = t.phases[1].augmentations[0];
    std::print("\nActual second path left stack {}; right endpoints {}; returned left partners {}; final " "size {}; minimum-cover left {}; right {}.\n",
               path.left, path.right, t.run.result.match_left,
               t.run.result.size, t.run.cover_left, t.run.cover_right);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d(65, 1100);
    dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle style;
    style.width = 2.5;
    style.height = 2.;
    style.font_size = 22;
    d.node("l0", {0, 0}, std::format("Free L{}", path.left[0]), style).node(
        "r0", {4.5, 0}, std::format("R{}", path.right[0]), style).node(
        "l1", {9, 0}, std::format("L{}", path.left[1]), style).node(
        "r1", {13.5, 0}, std::format("Free R{}", path.right[1]), style).edge(
        "l0", "r0", "insert").edge("r0", "l1", "remove").edge("l1", "r1",
                                                              "insert").text(
        {6.75, 2.5}, "Actual second-phase path: two inserts minus one removal",
        24).save_svg("build/hopcroft_karp_tiny.svg");
    if (path.left.size() != 2 || t.run.result.size != 2 ||
        t.run.result.match_left != std::vector<std::size_t>{1, 0})
        throw std::runtime_error("tiny augmentation");
}
