> Correct the shortest-path cutoff, not the optimum definition

The older BFS detected whether any augmentation existed, but its DFS accepted a
free right endpoint at any depth. On the public six-by-six regression fixture
below, frozen instrumentation of that original C++ implementation found a
second-phase shortest distance of 3 forward pairs while its chosen path had 4.
Both implementations return cardinality 6; the defect was the mismatch with the
stated shortest blocking-phase invariant and its analysis.

The corrected trace has a second-phase path with exactly 3 forward pairs. The
plotted matching size includes the terminal BFS; shortest-path points include
only successful phases. Captured finite labels can include an already discovered
cutoff frontier that BFS never expands. SIZE_MAX labels mean undiscovered and
are displayed as unseen.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hopcroft_karp_cutoff.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/hopcroft_karp_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    const auto g = dm::algorithms::hopcroft_karp_cutoff_graph();
    const auto t =
        dm::algorithms::hopcroft_karp_trace(g.n_left, g.n_right, g.edges);
    std::vector<double> calls, sizes, successful, shortest;
    std::size_t size = 0;
    std::print("| BFS call | pre-DFS left labels | shortest forward pairs | actual path sizes | matching " "size after phase |\n| ---: | --- | ---: | --- | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &phase : t.phases) {
        std::vector<std::string> labels;
        std::vector<std::size_t> lengths;
        for (auto d : phase.left_distance)
            labels.push_back(d == dm::algorithms::kBipartiteUnmatched ? "unseen"
                             : std::to_string(d));
        for (const auto &p : phase.augmentations) {
            lengths.push_back(p.left.size());
            ++size;
            if (p.left.size() != phase.shortest_pairs)
                throw std::runtime_error("nonshortest path");
        }
        calls.push_back(phase.bfs_index);
        sizes.push_back(size);
        if (phase.shortest_pairs) {
            successful.push_back(phase.bfs_index);
            shortest.push_back(phase.shortest_pairs);
        }
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", phase.bfs_index, labels,
                   phase.shortest_pairs, lengths, size);
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(calls, sizes, "matching size", {37, 99, 235}, 2.).points(
        successful, shortest, "shortest pairs", {220, 38, 38}, 6.).title(
        "Corrected cutoff: actual shortest paths only").x_label(
        "BFS call, final call is terminal").y_label("pairs").y_limits(0, 9).save_svg("build/hopcroft_karp_cutoff.svg");
    if (t.phases[1].shortest_pairs != 3 ||
        t.phases[1].augmentations[0].left.size() != 3 || t.run.result.size != 6)
        throw std::runtime_error("cutoff regression");
}
```
