\caption(The current curve uses producing records only. The historical four-pair path is documented as a frozen old-kernel observation, not drawn as a current measurement.)
\alttext(Matching size rises from5 to6 and remains6 at the terminal BFS; successful-phase shortest pair counts are1 and3.)

A maximum matching need not be unique. Across all 65536 four-by-four simple
graphs, frozen cardinalities agree before and after this change, while 3767
ordered matching choices differ. The original five-by-four fixture retains both
orientation arrays. The stable public result layout and maximum-cardinality
contract are preserved; arbitrary older tie choices are not a uniqueness
guarantee.

> Actual work and long paths without recursive stack growth

The ordered chain family has n vertices on each side. For each i below n-1,
supply (i,i) then (i,i+1), followed by (n-1,0). For n at least2, the first phase
matches n-1 direct pairs, and the second uses an alternating path with n forward
pairs to fill the final slot. This is a two-phase family, not a worst-case
example attaining the square-root phase bound.

Selected producing visits are 4n-2 BFS edge examinations, 3n-1 DFS edge
examinations and 2n-1 path-pair writes in this family. Each pair write assigns
both orientation arrays. Initialization, adjacency allocation/copying, queue
allocation, cover extraction and capture copies are outside these counters. The
deepest explicit left stack has n vertices. A separate native test exercises
n=20000 under ASan/UBSan; it does not rely on the process's recursive-call
stack.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/hopcroft_karp_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/hopcroft_karp_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <algorithm>
#include <filesystem>
#include <format>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<double> x, bfs, dfs, writes;
    std::print("| vertices per side | edges | matching size | successful phases | BFS edges | DFS edges | " "path-pair writes | max left-stack size |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: " "| ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t n : {2, 8, 32, 128, 512, 2048}) {
        const auto g = dm::algorithms::hopcroft_karp_chain_graph(n);
        const auto r =
            dm::algorithms::hopcroft_karp_run(g.n_left, g.n_right, g.edges);
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", n,
                   g.edges.size(), r.result.size, r.augmenting_phases,
                   r.work.bfs_edges, r.work.dfs_edges,
                   r.work.path_pairs_written, r.work.max_path_left_vertices);
        x.push_back(n);
        bfs.push_back(r.work.bfs_edges);
        dfs.push_back(r.work.dfs_edges);
        writes.push_back(r.work.path_pairs_written);
        if (r.result.size != n || r.augmenting_phases != 2 ||
            r.work.bfs_edges != 4 * n - 2 || r.work.dfs_edges != 3 * n - 1 ||
            r.work.path_pairs_written != 2 * n - 1 ||
            r.work.max_path_left_vertices != n)
            throw std::runtime_error("chain producing counts");
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(x, bfs, "BFS edges", {37, 99, 235}, 2.).line(x, dfs, "DFS edges",
                                                        {220, 38, 38}, 2.).line(
        x, writes, "pair writes", {22, 163, 74}, 2.).title(
        "Ordered chains: selected actual work in two successful phases").x_label("vertices per side").y_label("selected visits or pair writes").y_limits(0, 10000).save_svg("build/hopcroft_karp_work.svg");
}
```
